  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Today is the start of our annual end-of-year fundraising drive. Year after year, more than half of our entire annual operating budget has been raised around these final few weeks of the year. For the third year in a row, an amazingly generous donor is matching dollar-for-dollar the first $100,000 raised. Make your contributions early to have them doubled!</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We count on your giving-season generosity to make a tax-deductible donation to keep NutritionFacts.org going and growing.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I may be the face of NutritionFacts.org, but a veritable army of volunteers and now more than a dozen full-time </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/team/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">staff</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> members work tirelessly behind the scenes. They help me churn through thousands of studies to stay on top of the science and produce videos, articles, webinars, infographics, guides, and much more, so we can bring you the latest in evidence-based nutrition. Access to even just a single academic database, like Web of Science, can cost up to $16,000 a year. The work we do is only possible because of you.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every year, thousands of people step forward and make donations large and small to express appreciation for our work. Hundreds have even signed up to be monthly donors, which helps ensure a predictable and steady stream of support. Please “root” for the facts by helping us </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">fill the carrot</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">! It’s a numbers game; a donation of any amount truly helps.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">On the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Donate Page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, you can make a tax-deductible donation </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">using a credit card</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">,</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">PayPal, ACH, Google Pay, or Apple Pay</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. There is also an option for transferring </span><a href=\"https://www.stockdonator.com/stock-information/?oid=c9fe74\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">stock</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, or you can simply send a check to NutritionFacts.org at 6800 Wisconsin Avenue #1185 Chevy Chase, MD 20815. Federal employees can even donate through the CFC workplace giving program with designation number 26461.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Thank you so much for your support!</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Recipe: Baked Grain Loaf with Umami Sauce</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> <a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo.jpg/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-91047 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-1024x884.jpg\" alt=\"baked grain loaf\" width=\"200\" height=\"172\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-1024x884.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-960x829.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-768x663.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-1536x1326.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-1200x1036.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-720x622.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo-540x466.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-photo.jpg 1994w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>This versatile loaf is a perfect green-light main course for your holiday dinner table. I like to use whatever grains I have on hand––usually my </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/basic-brol-barley-rye-oats-and-lentils/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Basic BROL</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">!––and pair this loaf with a side of steamed greens, sweet potatoes, and assorted veggies. Get the free recipe on </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/baked-grain-loaf-with-umami-gravy-recipe-healthy-recipes-at-nutritionfacts-org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NutritionFacts.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and watch a video on how it’s made on our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CcDZgzhg93k/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Key Takeaways: Alcohol</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/alcohol.jpg/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-91045 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/alcohol.jpg\" alt=\"bottles of alcoholic beverages\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\"/></a>The holidays are a time for celebrating and, for many, that includes cocktails, beer, and wine. But regular consumption of alcohol has some potentially serious side effects…besides the hangover. See how alcohol can impact long-term outlooks on liver health and cancer on our </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/alcohol//\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4><b>Impact Story: Jay S.  </b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/jay-pic-large.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-91049 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/jay-pic-large.jpg\" alt=\"Jay S\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/jay-pic-large.jpg 596w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/jay-pic-large-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/12/jay-pic-large-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>I love hearing stories of how my work has changed people’s lives. Thank you to Jay for sending in his transformative story. </span></p>\n<p><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">“I am a 25-year-old graduate engineering student, originally from India, but I have lived in the UK and USA for about six years now. I have been a vegetarian all my life. I consider myself one of the fittest guys in my peer group, playing soccer for four years at the collegiate level, and I recently completed a half marathon. Soon after, I got my first ever lipid panel test done just because I thought I should have a data point of my health. The results were shocking. My total cholesterol was 286, LDL 168, and triglycerides 402. I was in disbelief. How can someone who runs four times a week and plays soccer have such bad numbers?</span></em></p>\n<p><em><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Through a family friend, I came across the book </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Die</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. I read that book in two days and listened to every single talk Dr. Greger has on the internet. Soon after, I started following a strict whole food, plant-based diet. I got my lipid panel done again after just two weeks, and all of my numbers improved dramatically: Total cholesterol went from 286 to 230, LDL from 168 to 144, and triglycerides from 402 to 236. I am so thankful to Dr. Greger for his public service, and I have recommended all my friends get a copy of his book and open their eyes to the junk they are eating.”</span></em></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Top Three Videos</b></h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-89187 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Gluten-free grains in bowls\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-21-the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-potential-harm-in-unnecessary-gluten-free-diets/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The Potential Harm in Unnecessary Gluten-Free Diets</span></a> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">– How might we prevent the inflammation from gluten-free diets?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-89381 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Assorted fruits and vegetables on counter\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-22-how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-to-naturally-reduce-wrinkles-with-food/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How to Naturally Reduce Wrinkles with Food</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> – Almonds are put to the test in a ​​randomized controlled trial for facial wrinkles.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-89413 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Group of runners\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2022/09/59-26-why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/why-all-athletes-should-eat-plant-based-diets/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why All Athletes Should Eat Plant-Based Diets</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> – Enhance athletic performance with diet.</span></p>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4> </h4>\n<h4><b>Live Q&amp;A</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-53879 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"Live Q&amp;A\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Every month, I do a live Q&amp;A right from my treadmill, and the next one is today, December 15!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At 3 pm ET, tune in on our </span><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Facebook</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> page, </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">YouTube</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> channel, or (new!) directly on </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NutritionFacts.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can find links to past live Q&amp;As </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on NutritionFacts.org.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>"
